    "abstract": "MobileNetV3 is tuned to mobile CPUs through hardware-aware network architecture search (platform-aware NAS plus NetAdapt) complemented by manual improvements: a redesigned efficient last stage, the h-swish nonlinearity, and squeeze-and-excite with hard-sigmoid. MobileNetV3-Large is 3.2% more accurate on ImageNet than MobileNetV2 while reducing latency by 20%; MobileNetV3-Small is 6.6% more accurate with comparable latency. A new LR-ASPP segmentation decoder is also proposed.",
    "domain": "CV",
    "key_claims": [
      "MobileNetV3-Large is 3.2% more accurate on ImageNet than MobileNetV2 while reducing latency by 20%.",
      "MobileNetV3-Small is 6.6% more accurate than MobileNetV2 at comparable latency.",
      "h-swish, x * ReLU6(x+3)/6, approximates swish with lower cost on mobile hardware.",
      "Moving the final 1x1 expansion after global pooling (efficient last stage) saves about 7 ms (11% of runtime) with no accuracy loss.",
      "MobileNetV3-Large reaches 75.2% and MobileNetV3-Small 67.4% ImageNet top-1."
    ],
